    "detailed_description": "In the year 20XX, when Japan's food culture has declined, the last remaining sushi chef rises up!<br>Opening a sushi restaurant with only one person!<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.poster.avif?t=1658235952\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.webm?t=1658235952\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.mp4?t=1658235952\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br>\u25a0 Story<br>20XX, Japanese food culture is fading.<br>My father, the last sushi craftsman in Japan, was unexpectedly hospitalized.<br>His words to me were, &quot;Take care of the rest!&quot;.<br>And then, the one-man operation conveyor belt sushi business suddenly starts!<br><br>\u25a0 Game<br>- Run a sushi restaurant in 60 seconds per game<br>- Offer sushi according to the customers' orders<br>- Increase your restaurant's rating by delivering fresh sushi as soon as possible<br>- Aim for high scores when your restaurant's rating ups and more customers come.<br><br>\u25a0 Restaurants<br>- Prefectures across Japan become the motif for the restaurants <br>- Each restaurant has a different gimmick reflecting its local impression<br><br>\u25a0 Sushi<br>- In addition to the basic Nigiri and Gunkan sushi, each restaurant offers sushi that looks like a local specialty.<br>- Level up sushi using EXP you earned from offering sushi<br><br>\u25a0 Avatars<br>- Change your sushi craftsman's outfit freely with avatar items available in the game<br><br>\u25a0 Partners<br>- Bring partners available in the game to the restaurant and activate skills that can benefit you<br>- A variety of local partners available",
    "about_the_game": "In the year 20XX, when Japan's food culture has declined, the last remaining sushi chef rises up!<br>Opening a sushi restaurant with only one person!<br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.poster.avif?t=1658235952\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.webm?t=1658235952\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2063010/extras/65188a7a2689a541741dc0983afadb38.mp4?t=1658235952\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br>\u25a0 Story<br>20XX, Japanese food culture is fading.<br>My father, the last sushi craftsman in Japan, was unexpectedly hospitalized.<br>His words to me were, &quot;Take care of the rest!&quot;.<br>And then, the one-man operation conveyor belt sushi business suddenly starts!<br><br>\u25a0 Game<br>- Run a sushi restaurant in 60 seconds per game<br>- Offer sushi according to the customers' orders<br>- Increase your restaurant's rating by delivering fresh sushi as soon as possible<br>- Aim for high scores when your restaurant's rating ups and more customers come.<br><br>\u25a0 Restaurants<br>- Prefectures across Japan become the motif for the restaurants <br>- Each restaurant has a different gimmick reflecting its local impression<br><br>\u25a0 Sushi<br>- In addition to the basic Nigiri and Gunkan sushi, each restaurant offers sushi that looks like a local specialty.<br>- Level up sushi using EXP you earned from offering sushi<br><br>\u25a0 Avatars<br>- Change your sushi craftsman's outfit freely with avatar items available in the game<br><br>\u25a0 Partners<br>- Bring partners available in the game to the restaurant and activate skills that can benefit you<br>- A variety of local partners available",
    "short_description": "Open a sushi restaurant with only one person! Many local-image store stages, sushi, and souvenirs throughout Nippon!",
